            <ArticleTitle>Symptom relief in palliative care.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>64-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Palliative medicine in hospice is emerging as a growing discipline, committed to holistic and compassionate, comforting care for seriously ill patients. It is essential to include aggressive medical therapy for pain relief; even more important to the issue is that the patient be the central figure in decisions of care.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
